Z||000000||DXR_DAD||11-06-1999||04:30 PM||||Ok it's #2 for the DXR family I just got a Blue 87 Coupe. The car is in ok condition, runs good. But here's the thing, start the car and no tach! 1-2 min it hits 1g, rev it to 2-3g's and it drops to 500 this only happens when it's cold.... first started. And it almost stalls.  I need help!! Where do I start?????||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||11-07-1999||04:59 AM||||I'd start first with the tach filter and maybe check all the engine ground wires too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||11-07-1999||11:18 AM||||Thanks Batboy, This 4cyl DIS is all new to me my 86SE v6 was easy. Where is the tach filter located on this thing? Do you mean the engine ground straps?||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||11-07-1999||11:18 AM||||I believe there is an idle adjustment on the 4-Bangers.  You're best off getting a good shop manual like a Chiltons or Haynes.  I always start with a good tune-up before anything else.  Make sure the timing is set correctly, and all the plugs and wires are in good shape.  I'd just get the easy stuff out of the way, because it could probably use a good tune-up anyways. You may also want to check the EGR system.  When the engine is warm, put your finger underneath the EGR valve and push up on that diaphragm.  When you push it a little, the engine idle should slow down, but if the diaphragm won't move, the EGR valve is probably shot.  Also get yourself a vacuum gauage and hook it up to a vacuum port on the manifold to see how much the engine "sucks."  It's an excellent way to check for vacuum leaks.  good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroshop||11-07-1999||11:26 AM||||Well I guess congradulations are in order, but it means a lot of work and knowing you I bet it'll be like your 86SE. Good luck.||||reg||10
